# Answer key for B10 t4_adversarial.sql - lexical robustness, adversarial.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all earlier decisions, plus D-35..D-38 (decided 2026-10-04, not
# implemented). standard_conforming_strings is on. NOT EXPRESSIBLE IN A KEY, CHECKED IN
# THE REPORT: S6, S12 (PREPARE) and S14 (DEALLOCATE ALL) are counted with no edges; S16
# is refused or declared, never resolved to a guessed table.

@ 16 S1 a dollar tag that spells a column
value staging.orders.currency -> mart.kpi_rollup.level derived
forbid value staging.orders.channel -> mart.kpi_rollup.level derived | o.channel is the text of a dollar-quoted literal

@ 24 S2 E'' escapes hide c.email inside the literal
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.full_name derived
forbid value staging.customers.email -> mart.top_customers.full_name derived | c.email is between escaped quotes, inside one E'' literal

@ 32 S3 a standard string ending in a backslash
value staging.customers.email -> mart.customer_summary.full_name derived

@ 40 S4 -- glued to an operand
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix.revenue identity
forbid value staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix.revenue derived | --1 is a comment, not minus minus one

@ 49 S5 a nested comment
value staging.customers.id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.top_customers.region identity
forbid value staging.customers.email -> mart.top_customers.region identity | c.email is inside the nested comment, which a non-nesting lexer would end early
forbid value staging.customers.email -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity | the INSERT after S5 is inside a nested comment

@ 70 S7 EXECUTE p_lit: '$2' is text
value staging.customers.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.country_code identity
filter staging.customers.segment, staging.customers.email -> mart.kpi_rollup

@ 77 S8 :: casts and a [1:2] slice beside :lo
value staging.orders.tags, staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix.channel derived
filter staging.orders.id -> mart.channel_mix

@ 86 S9 quoted identifiers containing /* and --
value staging.customers.email -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
filter staging.customers.status -> mart.top_customers

@ 98 S10 a U&"" identifier spelling id
value staging.customers.id -> mart.kpi_rollup.customers identity

@ 106 S11 EXECUTE before PREPARE
expect source_unavailable p_late | S11: p_late is prepared only at S12 (D-35)

@ 122 S13 EXECUTE after PREPARE
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.channel_mix.region identity
filter core.dim_store.status -> mart.channel_mix

@ 134 S15 EXECUTE after DEALLOCATE ALL
expect source_unavailable p_lit | S15: DEALLOCATE ALL at S14 forgot p_lit (D-35); S7's edges must not be emitted again here

@ 141 S16 a psql variable as an identifier
forbid value staging.orders.channel -> mart.kpi_rollup.level identity | :tbl cannot be resolved by the analysis; refused or declared, never guessed (D-36)

@ 149 S17 dollar quotes glued to operators
value staging.orders.id -> mart.sales_daily.orders identity
filter staging.orders.status, staging.orders.channel, staging.orders.discount_code -> mart.sales_daily

@ 158 S18 E'a\\' ends after the escaped backslash
value staging.customers.email -> mart.customer_summary.segment derived

@ 166 S19 an identifier containing $
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
